        "date": "2026-11-12T01:00:44Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): drill reach, cross drill and probe stylus read the body's band stack\n\nThe three laws #835 left on the cylinder enclosing a modelled tool body\nnow read the band stack the simulation draws: the axial holder-face law\nand cross_holder check each band's face disc / swept footprint against\nthe material over that band's radius, cross_part::part_clear takes the\nbody-carrying cutter, and probe_op::stylus_cutter is rebuilt as stem +\nprobe body + the body's bands. A stepped body whose flange never reaches\nthe material is no longer refused; one whose flange does is, naming the\nband. No body (or a stack that does not fit) reads the holder cylinder\nbit-identically; the enclosure wording stays only for that fallback.\n\nStacked on #957 (issue #852).\n\nFixes #842\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
